## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical data quality, governance, rollback, and per-tenant isolation on GCP, with real components like Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery, Cloud Storage, Data Catalog, and time-travel. It also tests how to surface quality signals to dashboards and maintain lineage.

## Key Concepts

- Data quality framework per tenant (schema conformance, null checks, dedupe)
- Per-tenant isolation in BigQuery
- Data Catalog lineage and contract testing
- Rollback using BigQuery time travel and snapshots
- Testing strategy and drift monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Sample validation stub for a record
function validate(rec){
  if(!rec.tenant_id) throw new Error("missing tenant_id");
  if(rec.event_time == null) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement per-tenant rollback with time travel and ensure consistency across dashboards?
- How would you scale the quality checks as tenants grow from 4 to 100+?

## Why This Is Asked
Understanding end-to-end streaming ingestion, privacy handling, and basic rollback in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming
- Dataflow DoFn masking
- BigQuery per-tenant datasets
- Data Catalog data contracts and lineage
- Quarantine path and 24h rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow DoFn: mask PII before write
class MaskPIIFn {
  process(element) {
    // element is a JSON object
    if (element.email) element.email = maskEmail(element.email);
    if (element.phone) element.phone = maskPhone(element.phone);
    return element;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this pipeline for schema drift and masking correctness?
- How would you alert on quarantine volume spikes and auto-remediate?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes design for per-tenant data quality and schema evolution in a large-scale streaming pipeline, focusing on data catalog lineage, backward-compatible changes, drift detection, and rollback – all essential for production data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming data quality checks (null density, ranges, referential integrity)
- Per-tenant isolation in storage and compute
- Schema evolution with backward compatibility
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog
- Drift detection and tenant-specific rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal validator against a registry schema (conceptual)
function validateRecord(record, schema) {
  // assume 'schema' is loaded from Data Catalog
  const valid = ajv.validate(schema, record);
  if (!valid) throw new Error('Validation error: ' + ajv.errorsText());
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to test schema drift across tenants and automate remediation?
- How to handle late-arriving data and replays without breaking lineage?
- How to enforce tenant isolation at storage and compute layers?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a candidate's ability to implement a straightforward streaming ingestion with validation, error handling, and rollback using familiar GCP primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub ingestion and Dataflow (Beam)
- JSON schema validation and field filtering
- BigQueryIO writes with insertId for idempotency and daily partitioning
- Dead-letter handling and Cloud Storage archival
- Lightweight testing and rollback planning

## Code Example
```javascript
function validate(record){
  if (typeof record.user_id !== 'string') return false;
  if (typeof record.event_time !== 'string') return false;
  if (typeof record.event_type !== 'string') return false;
  return true;
}
```

